# One regular expression per line, matched against the full URL.
# Add a short reason above every entry.

# The Markdown headings in README.md start with an emoji. GitHub keeps the
# invisible variation selector (U+FE0F) in the generated anchor, so the table of
# contents links look like #%EF%B8%8F-screenshots and do work on GitHub (checked
# against the HTML GitHub renders for README.md). lychee removes the selector
# when it builds the heading ids, so it wrongly reports these as missing.
%EF%B8%8F

# GitHub answers 404 to anonymous requests for /stargazers on every repository
# (also on cli/cli), so the badge link in README.md can't be checked here.
^https://github\.com/Muskankr/OpenSourceMate/stargazers$

# platform.openai.com sits behind a bot filter and answers 403 to automated
# requests. The page itself is public.
^https://platform\.openai\.com/$
